<title>USA: U.S. Dec housing starts fell 12.2 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Dec housing starts fell 12.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and</p>
<p>building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> PCT CHANGE: Dec     Nov (Prev)     Oct (Prev)   Dec96/95</p>
<p> -Starts   -12.2     9.3    9.2    -5.2   -5.1	 -6.7</p>
<p> -Permits   -0.6     4.1    3.9    -2.6   -2.6	 -5.2</p>
<p> RATES	 Dec     Nov (Prev)     Oct (Prev)   Dec 1995</p>
<p> -Starts   1,329   1,514  1,514   1,385  1,386	1,425</p>
<p> -Permits  1,410   1,418  1,415   1,362  1,362	1,487</p>
<p> STARTS:     Dec     Nov (Prev)     Oct (Prev)   Dec 1995</p>
<p> -Single   1,024   1,161  1,164   1,088  1,082	1,150</p>
<p> -Multiple   305     353    350     297    304	  275</p>
<p> PERMITS     Dec     Nov (Prev)     Oct (Prev)   Dec 1995</p>
<p> -Single   1,016   1,025  1,027   1,011  1,011	1,123</p>
<p> -Multiple   394     393    388     351    351	  364</p>
<p> DEC STARTS--Pct--Rate    DEC PERMITS--Pct---Rate--------</p>
<p> -Northeast -2.3   125    -Northeast   5.9   143</p>
<p> -Midwest   -7.9   302    -Midwest     0.3   314</p>
<p> -South     -7.2   645    -South	-1.2   633</p>
<p> -West     -29.2   257    -West	 -2.7   320</p>
<p>Actual Starts and Permits, unadjusted in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	  Dec     Nov (Prev)     Oct (Prev)   Dec 1995</p>
<p>  Starts	90     112    111     131    131	   93</p>
<p>  Permits     99     102    101     126    126	   97</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast December starts at a 1.47 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>Housing starts for all of 1996 were at a rate of 1.474 million units, the highest annual rate since 1.488 million in 1988, the department said.</p>
<p>The level of housing starts in the West fell to its lowest rate since February 1993, when it was also 257,000.</p>
